The rejections stem from "lease lost before completion" retries that began accumulating shortly after 11:04 UTC. Checking all configuration changes in the two-hour window before the first rejection (09:41–11:41 UTC) across every component, only one change plausibly explains workers losing their leases mid-job: amber-ocr's `worker.lease_seconds` was slashed from 600 seconds to 45 seconds at 11:04 UTC. With a 45-second lease, workers simply ran out of time before finishing pages-heavy OCR jobs, causing repeated lease losses, retries, and ultimately rejections after 5 failed attempts (first one at 11:41:49.157). No other component had any change in that window that would produce this failure mode (ember-index's 11:31 change only adjusts commit interval, unrelated to amber-ocr's leasing).

```json
{
  "faulty_change": "CHG-67658"
}
```

